    "title": "WIU bilingual learning center, Moline, gives lessons in English and Spanish - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gavin Waidelich ,\n1 hours ago\nWestern Illinois University. is expanding its student base to include those first learning their ABCs in English and Spanish. The WIU Bilingual Early Learning and Family Center in Moline opened earlier this fall, but officially cut the ribbon Wednesday.\nThe center accepts kids ages 15 months to five years old. College students also get to learn there too.\n“With early learning or early childhood education being a significant need for the Quad Cities area, this was an opportunity to both provide for the area and create some experiential learning opportunities for our WIU education students,” said WIU President Kristi Mindrup.\nThe center is in the Floreciente neighborhood, which has a large Spanish-speaking community. One woman says the bilingual lessons are helping her granddaughter find her voice.\n“She actually began to say some things at home that surprised me, because I would try to talk to her and she would just shy away,” said Consuelo Lopez. “Now that she’s coming here, she’s more open and beginning to talk more in Spanish and it’s just very, very exciting.”\nInstructions start in English and then kids are taught in a mix of both languages.\n“If you can communicate with a friend in English, but also with a friend in French, and a friend in Spanish, then you will have more friends,” said Eduardo Perez, director of the education center. “Regardless of where we come from or what language we speak at home, we all have common areas that we all meet.”\nThe center currently serves fewer than 20 students, with the capacity to serve 75. For more information, visit here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHBF - OurQuadCities.com.",
